WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.999
This is Anna, a commercial banker with one real question. A client wants a loan, and she needs a credit memo.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.999
She could just ask plain AI, but plain AI is a genius with amnesia. It doesn't know her bank, and it forgets her.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.999
So her request goes to the brain instead. And the brain isn't magic. It's a platform, running in the bank's own cloud.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:36.999
Inside it, a library of skills, a memory of every decision and governed connections into the bank's systems. Only the reasoning model at the core is rented.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.999
So when Anna's ask arrives, the brain reads it and hands it to the right specialist, the credit memo agent.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.999
That agent runs on the bank's own judgment, encoded as skills, and it reaches into her systems as Anna, never beyond her clearance.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.999
To ground its answer, it retrieves by meaning. Vector search finds the policy and the past deals that resemble this one.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.999
It retrieves by relationship, a knowledge graph linking borrower, guarantor, and exposure, and the hard numbers straight from the bank's records.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.999
It reasons on Claude and forms a judgment, cited, never invented. Every step is logged.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.999
The model proposes. A person decides.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:31.999
Minutes later, Anna has her draft, sourced, governed, ready for committee, and her decision becomes a new skill, so the whole bank gets sharper.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:43.999
And the memo is just one example. Customer 360, spreading, regulatory questions. Every ask finds its specialist in the same brain.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.999
That is why you need a brain. The model is rented. The knowledge is owned.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.570
Commercial credit. Reinvented.
